<!--
  THE MARK: M and A cut from one graphite line, with a packet of light travelling between them.
  Two readings, both true at once: a wordmark (M•A), and traffic entering the M's notch and leaving
  through the A's arch - which is the product. The "A" keeps an arch where a normal A keeps a bar,
  so the two letters rhyme: entrance / exit.

  Authored on the 24-unit grid (bbox x 2.8..21.8, y 7.2..17.8, stroke 2.0 of 24) and scaled x3.45
  into the 108 adaptive canvas: the wordmark is 19 units wide, so 3.45 lands it at ~66dp - inside the
  66% safe zone of every launcher mask, with the mark's own optical centre on the canvas centre.
-->
